; themes.eval - painting with a surface THEME (docs/editor-themes-notes.md).
;
; tools/EditorTest.py writes the theme into the project's themes.cat
; before this runs (and restores the project after):
;
;   [marble_hall]  floor = floor_rubble   wall = wall_marble
;                  ceiling = ceiling_stone
;
; floor_rubble is NOT in eval_arena's palette - painting must enrol it.
;
; The script carves room A (x 1..7, z 1..22) off the arena as areafill.eval
; does, area-fills it with the theme, and reads squares back with
; `editor cell`: each surface's STORED value (theme:<id> = a reference to the
; theme) and the texture it resolves to, which must be its member.
; Then the round trip: savemap, leave, come back - the references survive.

logecho on
reset
editor fill walls wall_marble rect 8 1 26 22
geomhash
echo --- area fill with the theme ---
editor fill themes marble_hall area 3 3
geomhash
editor cell 1 1
editor cell 3 3
editor cell 7 22
editor cell 5 12
editor cell 0 5
editor cell 8 9
echo --- the eyedropper picks up the theme ---
editor pick 4 4
echo --- saved, left and reloaded ---
savemap
goto crypt1
goto eval_arena
geomhash
editor cell 3 3
editor cell 0 5
echo --- a new theme from the selected square ---
; 1,5 is in room A beside the west wall: its floor, its ceiling and that
; wall seed the new theme, one member each - so a square painted with it
; must show exactly those.
editor cell 1 5
editor inspect 1 5
editor inspect off
newtype themes
editor fill themes theme1 area 3 3
editor cell 3 3
editor cell 0 9
